From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lasimeri <217267696+Lasimeri@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 23:24:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] x86/lib: cached copy instead of non-temporal stores on
 Knights Corner

__copy_user_nocache() is hand-written with MOVNTI and SFENCE, both SSE2
and absent on Knights Corner (ISA reference 327364, Appendix B). Under
X86_KNC assemble the same code with ordinary MOV and no fence: callers
of the "nocache" copy only lose the cache-bypass hint, the data path is
unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/x86/lib/copy_user_uncached_64.S | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/x86/lib/copy_user_uncached_64.S b/arch/x86/lib/copy_user_uncached_64.S
index 8ed0ce3ad..a81314202 100644
--- a/arch/x86/lib/copy_user_uncached_64.S
+++ b/arch/x86/lib/copy_user_uncached_64.S
@@ -7,6 +7,15 @@
 #include <linux/linkage.h>
 #include <linux/objtool.h>
 #include <asm/asm.h>
+#ifdef CONFIG_X86_KNC
+/*
+ * Knights Corner has no SSE2: MOVNTI and SFENCE are undefined (ISA
+ * reference 327364, Appendix B). The uncached copy becomes a cached one;
+ * every caller tolerates that, it only loses the cache-bypass hint.
+ */
+#define movnti mov
+#define sfence
+#endif
 
 /*
  * copy_user_nocache - Uncached memory copy with exception handling
